With the GPMs and the badges?

529
00:47:13,910 --> 00:47:17,990
Yeah, but can I tell you a secret?

530
00:47:18,580 --> 00:47:21,410
- No. - All right. Here it goes.

531
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:25,460
I never actually built a tent before. There! I said it.

532
00:47:26,050 --> 00:47:28,160
You've been camping before, haven't you?

533
00:47:28,260 --> 00:47:30,710
Well, never outside.

534
00:47:31,220 --> 00:47:34,630
Well, why didn't you ask your dad how to build a tent?

535
00:47:35,100 --> 00:47:37,930
I don't think he wants to talk about this stuff.

536
00:47:38,020 --> 00:47:40,630
Why don't you try him sometime. Maybe he'll surprise you.

537
00:47:40,730 --> 00:47:43,060
Well, he's away a lot. I don't see him much.

538
00:47:43,150 --> 00:47:44,760
He's gotta be home sometime.

539
00:47:44,860 --> 00:47:49,100
Well, I call, but Phyllis told me I bug him too much.

540
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:52,610
Phyllis? You call your own mother by her first name?

541
00:47:53,070 --> 00:47:54,860
Phyllis isn't my mom.

542
00:48:05,340 --> 00:48:09,420
But he promised he'd come to my Explorers Ceremony

543
00:48:09,510 --> 00:48:12,290
To pin on my Assisting The Elderly Badge.

544
00:48:13,590 --> 00:48:16,510
So, he can show me about tents then, right?

545
00:48:23,060 --> 00:48:25,680
Hey, why don t you get some sleep?

546
00:48:25,980 --> 00:48:29,600
Don't wanna wake up the traveling flea circus.

547
00:48:31,650 --> 00:48:33,140
Mr. Fredricksen,

548
00:48:33,240 --> 00:48:36,110
Dug says he wants to take Kevin prisoner.

549
00:48:36,990 --> 00:48:38,950
We have to protect him.

550
00:48:41,160 --> 00:48:43,200
Can Kevin go with us?

551
00:48:44,830 --> 00:48:46,750
All right, he can come.

552
00:48:47,420 --> 00:48:49,540
Promise you won't leave him?

553
00:48:50,050 --> 00:48:52,160
- Yeah. - Cross your heart?

554
00:49:00,720 --> 00:49:02,260
Cross my heart.

555
00:49:07,820 --> 00:49:10,310
What have I got myself into, Ellie?

556
00:49:33,510 --> 00:49:35,250
Good morning, sweetheart.

557
00:49:37,430 --> 00:49:39,010
We'd better get moving.

558
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:43,060
Bird's gone.

559
00:49:43,140 --> 00:49:46,730
Maybe Russell won't notice. All right, everybody up!

560
00:49:47,560 --> 00:49:49,450
Where's Kevin? He's wondered off!

561
00:49:49,450 --> 00:49:52,020
Kevin! Dug, find Kevin!

562
00:49:52,110 --> 00:49:55,940
Find the bird, find the bird! Point!

563
00:49:56,030 --> 00:49:57,900
Look! There he is.

564
00:50:00,330 --> 00:50:01,490
Point!

565
00:50:01,870 --> 00:50:05,530
Hey, that's my food! Get off my roof!

566
00:50:05,620 --> 00:50:06,860
Yeah, get off of his roof!

567
00:50:12,460 --> 00:50:13,540
What is it doing?

568
00:50:13,630 --> 00:50:16,040
The bird is calling to her babies.

569
00:50:17,180 --> 00:50:18,630
Her babies!

570
00:50:20,010 --> 00:50:21,550
Kevin is a girl?

571
00:50:23,930 --> 00:50:26,680
Her house s over there in those twisty rocks.

572
00:50:27,770 --> 00:50:30,010
She has been gathering food for her babies

573
00:50:30,010 --> 00:50:31,350
And must get back to them.

574
00:50:32,610 --> 00:50:34,270
Wait, Kevin is just leaving.

575
00:50:36,860 --> 00:50:39,350
But you promised to protect her.

576
00:50:39,450 --> 00:50:42,740
Her babies need her. We gotta make sure they're together.

577
00:50:42,830 --> 00:50:45,860
Sorry, Russell. We've lost enough time already.

578
00:50:47,330 --> 00:50:48,450
Yeah.

579
00:50:56,130 --> 00:50:58,840
This was her favorite chocolate.

580
00:50:59,470 --> 00:51:03,510
Because you sent her away, there's more for you.

581
00:51:06,310 --> 00:51:07,470
Kevin?

582
00:51:26,160 --> 00:51:29,070
Where's the bird? You said you had the bird!

583
00:51:29,160 --> 00:51:30,370
Oh, yes, oh, yes.

584
00:51:30,460 --> 00:51:33,490
Since I have said that, I can see how you would think that.

585
00:51:33,590 --> 00:51:36,670
- Where is it? - Uh.... Tomorrow.

586
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:40,620
Come back tomorrow, and then I will again have the bird. Yes.

587
00:51:41,890 --> 00:51:45,550
You lost it. Why do I not have a surprised feeling?

588
00:51:46,100 --> 00:51:49,340
Well, at least you now have led us to the small mailman

589
00:51:49,440 --> 00:51:51,930
And the one who smells of prunes.

590
00:51:53,610 --> 00:51:56,100
The master will be most pleased we have found them.

591
00:51:56,190 --> 00:51:59,100
He will ask them many questions. Come.

592
00:51:59,190 --> 00:52:01,380
Wait! We're not going with you.

593
00:52:01,390 --> 00:52:02,730
We're going to the falls!

594
00:52:05,240 --> 00:52:06,360
Get away from me!

595
00:52:10,160 --> 00:52:11,500
Get down!

596
00:53:05,840 --> 00:53:06,920
Stay!

597
00:53:15,150 --> 00:53:17,730
You came here in that?

598
00:53:18,230 --> 00:53:19,470
Uh, yeah.

599
00:53:20,230 --> 00:53:24,070
In a house? A floating house?

600
00:53:32,580 --> 00:53:35,410
That is the darnest thing I've ever seen!

601
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:38,540
You're not after my bird, are you?

602
00:53:38,960 --> 00:53:41,500
But if you needed to borrow a cup of sugar

603
00:53:41,590 --> 00:53:43,830
I'd be happy to oblige.

604
00:53:47,220 --> 00:53:49,800
Well, this is all a misunderstanding.

605
00:53:50,260 --> 00:53:52,100
My dogs made a mistake.

606
00:53:52,680 --> 00:53:55,100
Wait. Are you Charles Muntz?

607
00:53:55,190 --> 00:53:57,800
Yeah, well, yes.

608
00:53:57,900 --> 00:54:00,010
The Charles Muntz?

609
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:02,310
Adventure's out there!

610
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:05,940
It's really him! That's Chares Muntz!

611
00:54:06,240 --> 00:54:09,610
- It is? Who's Charles Muntz? - Him!

612
00:54:11,620 --> 00:54:14,450
My wife and I, we were your biggest fans.

613
00:54:14,540 --> 00:54:16,280
Oh, well. You're a man of good taste.

614
00:54:18,630 --> 00:54:20,790
Now, you must be tired. Hungry?

615
00:54:20,880 --> 00:54:21,910
Uh-huh.

616
00:54:22,130 --> 00:54:23,460
Now, attention, everyone!

617
00:54:23,550 --> 00:54:27,380
These people are no longer intruders. They are our guests.

618
00:54:29,600 --> 00:54:31,960
Follow me. I Iike you temporarily.

619
00:54:32,060 --> 00:54:33,760
You do smile like prunes.

620
00:54:36,520 --> 00:54:37,630
I will not bite you.

621
00:54:37,730 --> 00:54:40,190
The small mailman smells like chocolate!

622
00:54:41,440 --> 00:54:43,600
I'm sorry about the dogs,

623
00:54:43,690 --> 00:54:46,680
- I hope they weren't too rough on you. - We weren't.

624
00:54:46,780 --> 00:54:50,240
Go ahead and moor your airship right next to mine.

625
00:54:55,870 --> 00:54:59,460
We are not actually going inside the Spirit of Adventure itself?

626
00:55:00,830 --> 00:55:02,420
Would you like to?

627
00:55:02,500 --> 00:55:03,740
Would I?

628
00:55:05,880 --> 00:55:07,750
Wait up, Mr. Muntz!

629
00:55:08,590 --> 00:55:10,130
Jiminy Cricket!

630
00:55:10,470 --> 00:55:12,510
- Not you! - What do we do with Dug?

631
00:55:12,600 --> 00:55:16,340
He lost the bird. Put him in the Cone of Shame.

632
00:55:21,310 --> 00:55:23,650
I do not like the Cone of Shame.

633
00:55:25,030 --> 00:55:29,270
Most of the collection is housed in the world's top museums.

634
00:55:29,360 --> 00:55:30,660
New York, Munich, London.

635
00:55:30,660 --> 00:55:33,110
Of course I kept the best for myself.

636
00:55:33,490 --> 00:55:36,330
Did you ever! WiII you Iook at that?

637
00:55:36,410 --> 00:55:38,900
Oh, yes, the Arsinoitherium.

638
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:41,700
Beast charged while I was brushing my teeth.

639
00:55:41,790 --> 00:55:44,530
Used my shaving kit to bring it down.

640
00:55:44,630 --> 00:55:46,330
Oh yeah. Well, surprise me.

641
00:55:46,420 --> 00:55:48,830
Only way to get it out of Ethiopia at the time

642
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:51,880
Was to have it declared as denta equipment.

643
00:55:52,300 --> 00:55:55,670
Oh, my gosh! The giant Somalian Somalian Labradodis!

644
00:55:55,760 --> 00:55:58,630
Oh, you recognize it? I'm impressed!

645
00:55:58,980 --> 00:56:01,010
There's an interesting story there.

646
00:56:01,440 --> 00:56:03,140
Excellent choice.

647
00:56:03,230 --> 00:56:07,020
I found it on safari with Roosevelt.

648
00:56:07,110 --> 00:56:08,940
He and I fell into a habit of

649
00:56:08,940 --> 00:56:10,980
Playing Gin Rummy in the evenings,

650
00:56:11,070 --> 00:56:12,900
And did he cheat!

651
00:56:12,990 --> 00:56:15,230
Oh, he was horrible.

652
00:56:15,870 --> 00:56:18,480
Master, dinner is ready.

653
00:56:18,830 --> 00:56:20,950
Oh, dear, broken translator.

654
00:56:21,040 --> 00:56:25,620
I think it's that loose wire again. There you go, big fellow.

655
00:56:25,710 --> 00:56:27,080
Thank you, Master.

656
00:56:27,170 --> 00:56:29,380
I liked his other voice.

657
00:56:30,590 --> 00:56:33,880
Well, dinner is served. Right this way.

658
00:56:35,010 --> 00:56:38,180
So, how are things States side, huh?

659
00:56:38,270 --> 00:56:40,680
Almost tempted to go back a few times.

660
00:56:41,730 --> 00:56:44,340
But I have unfinished work here.

661
00:56:44,440 --> 00:56:47,430
Please! I hope you're hungry.

662
00:56:47,520 --> 00:56:51,810
Because Epsilon is the finest chef I've ever had.

663
00:56:56,620 --> 00:56:59,610
Oh, Epsilon, you've done it again!

664
00:56:59,700 --> 00:57:00,740
Yes!

665
00:57:02,290 --> 00:57:04,280
Hey! Hey!

666
00:57:04,710 --> 00:57:07,750
Oh. My Ellie would have loved all these.

667
00:57:07,840 --> 00:57:10,290
You know its because of you she had this dream

668
00:57:10,380 --> 00:57:13,040
To come down here and ve by Paradise Falls.

669
00:57:13,130 --> 00:57:15,670
I'm honored. And now you've made it.

670
00:57:15,760 --> 00:57:18,220
You sure we're not bothering you? I'd hate to impose.

671
00:57:18,310 --> 00:57:21,200
No, no, it's a pleasure to have guests.

672
00:57:21,200 --> 00:57:22,340
A real treat.

673
00:57:22,430 --> 00:57:24,060
- Treat? - Where's my treat? I want my treat!

674
00:57:24,060 --> 00:57:26,970
No, no. Quiet! Calm down, calm down.

675
00:57:27,060 --> 00:57:28,470
- I want a treat! I want a treat! - Hey!

676
00:57:28,570 --> 00:57:30,150
I shouldn't have used that word.

677
00:57:30,230 --> 00:57:32,980
Having guests is a delight!

678
00:57:33,070 --> 00:57:36,940
More often I get thieves come to steal what is rightfully mine.

679
00:57:37,030 --> 00:57:38,070
No.

680
00:57:40,620 --> 00:57:43,080
They called me a fraud, those

681
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:47,680
But once I bring back this creature,

682
00:57:47,680 --> 00:57:49,580
My name will be cleared.

683
00:57:50,500 --> 00:57:52,460
Beautiful, isn't it?

684
00:57:55,130 --> 00:57:57,800
Oh, I've spent a lifetime tracking it.

685
00:57:59,760 --> 00:58:03,600
Sometimes years go by between sightings.

686
00:58:04,560 --> 00:58:09,140
I've tried to smoke it out of that death land where it lives.

687
00:58:09,980 --> 00:58:11,640
You can't go in after it.

688
00:58:12,150 --> 00:58:14,360
Once in, there's no way out.

689
00:58:14,990 --> 00:58:16,940
I lost so many dogs.

690
00:58:19,620 --> 00:58:21,550
And here they come, these bandits,

691
00:58:21,550 --> 00:58:24,110
And think the bird is theirs to take.

692
00:58:24,790 --> 00:58:27,560
But they soon found that this mountain

693
00:58:27,560 --> 00:58:29,830
Is a very dangerous place.

694
00:58:32,590 --> 00:58:34,670
Hey, that looks like Kevin.

695
00:58:36,720 --> 00:58:39,550
- Kevin? - Yeah, that's my new giant pet bird!

696
00:58:39,640 --> 00:58:41,720
I trained it to follow us.

697
00:58:41,810 --> 00:58:45,010
Follow you? It's impossible. How?

698
00:58:45,480 --> 00:58:47,930
- She likes chocolate. - Chocolate?

699
00:58:48,350 --> 00:58:51,940
Yeah. I gave hersome of my chocolate. She goes gaga for it.

700
00:58:52,020 --> 00:58:54,940
But it ran off. It's gone now.

701
00:59:01,780 --> 00:59:06,370
You know Carl, these people who pass through here,

702
00:59:06,460 --> 00:59:09,040
They all tell pretty good stories.

703
00:59:11,750 --> 00:59:13,990
A surveyor making a map.

704
00:59:15,840 --> 00:59:18,130
A botanist cataloguing plants.

705
00:59:21,220 --> 00:59:26,890
An old man taking his house to Paradise Falls.

706
00:59:33,440 --> 00:59:35,230
I mean that's the best one yet.

707
00:59:35,230 --> 00:59:37,560
I cant wait to hear how it ends.

708
00:59:47,200 --> 00:59:50,820
Well, it's been a wonderful evening, but we'd better be going.

709
00:59:50,920 --> 00:59:52,250
Oh, you're not leaving.

710
00:59:52,330 --> 00:59:55,950
We don't want to take advantage of your hospitality.

711
00:59:56,050 --> 00:59:57,050
Come on, Russell.

712
00:59:57,050 --> 00:59:59,250
But we haven't even had dessert yet.

713
00:59:59,340 --> 01:00:02,250
Oh, the boy is right. You haven't had dessert.

714
01:00:02,590 --> 01:00:06,960
Epsilon here makes a delicious cherries jubilee.

715
01:00:08,180 --> 01:00:11,270
Oh. You really must stay! I insist!

716
01:00:11,940 --> 01:00:14,270
We have so much more to talk about!

717
01:00:18,610 --> 01:00:19,770
Kevin?

718
01:00:27,490 --> 01:00:28,860
It's here.

719
01:00:31,080 --> 01:00:32,070
Get them!

720
01:00:34,840 --> 01:00:37,250
- Hurry! - I am hurrying!

721
01:00:37,340 --> 01:00:39,620
Ahhh! They're coming!

722
01:00:41,760 --> 01:00:44,340
Master! Over here!

723
01:00:59,820 --> 01:01:02,150
Go toward the light, Master!

724
01:01:31,020 --> 01:01:32,380
Russell!

725
01:01:36,860 --> 01:01:38,310
Get back!

726
01:01:41,030 --> 01:01:44,860
Go on, master! I will stop the dogs!

727
01:01:46,070 --> 01:01:47,690
Stop, you dogs!

728
01:02:16,060 --> 01:02:17,180
Help!

729
01:02:17,730 --> 01:02:19,010
Help!

730
01:02:19,480 --> 01:02:20,690
Help!

731
01:02:25,490 --> 01:02:27,230
Give me your hand!

732
01:02:38,580 --> 01:02:40,290
Hang on to Kevin!

733
01:03:11,870 --> 01:03:13,230
Kevin.

734
01:03:36,980 --> 01:03:40,890
No, no, no. Kevin. Stay down.

735
01:03:41,810 --> 01:03:46,180
She's hurt real bad. Can't we help her get home?

736
01:03:57,160 --> 01:03:59,740
All right, but we gotta hurry.

737
01:04:06,380 --> 01:04:07,870
You lost them?

738
01:04:07,960 --> 01:04:09,120
No, it was Dug.

739
01:04:09,220 --> 01:04:12,550
Yeah. He's with them. He helped them escape!

740
01:04:13,890 --> 01:04:14,970
Wait.

741
01:04:15,310 --> 01:04:18,470
Wait a minute. Dug.

742
01:04:24,480 --> 01:04:25,600
See anything?

743
01:04:25,690 --> 01:04:29,150
No, my pack is not following us. Boy, they are dumb.

744
01:04:29,440 --> 01:04:30,680
This is crazy.

745
01:04:30,780 --> 01:04:32,320
I finally meet my chidlhood hero,

746
01:04:32,320 --> 01:04:34,360
And he's trying to kill us. What a joke!

747
01:04:34,450 --> 01:04:35,810
Hey, I know a joke.

748
01:04:35,950 --> 01:04:37,820
A squirrel walks up to a tree and says,

749
01:04:37,950 --> 01:04:41,120
"I forgot to store acorns for winter and now I am dead".

750
01:04:41,210 --> 01:04:44,540
Ha! It s funny because the squirrel gets dead.

751
01:04:48,130 --> 01:04:49,870
Careful, Russell.

752
01:04:49,960 --> 01:04:51,550
You okay, Kevin?

753
01:04:56,640 --> 01:04:58,880
You know what, Mr. Fredricksen?

754
01:04:58,970 --> 01:05:01,840
The wilderness isn't quite what I expected.

755
01:05:01,980 --> 01:05:03,560
Yeah? How so?

756
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:06,140
It's kind of wild.

757
01:05:06,560 --> 01:05:09,900
I mean, it's not how they made it sound in my book.

758
01:05:09,980 --> 01:05:11,900
Get used to that, kid.

759
01:05:11,990 --> 01:05:14,400
My dad made it sound so easy.

760
01:05:14,490 --> 01:05:16,570
He is really good at camping,

761
01:05:16,660 --> 01:05:19,740
And how to make fire from rocks and stuff

762
01:05:19,830 --> 01:05:22,540
He used to come to all my squad lodge meetings.

763
01:05:23,210 --> 01:05:26,490
And afterwards, we go get icecream that fattens.

764
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:29,740
I always get chocolate and he gets butter brickle.

765
01:05:29,840 --> 01:05:32,800
Then we sit on this one curb, right outside

766
01:05:32,880 --> 01:05:36,720
And I'll count all the blue cars and he counts all the red ones,

767
01:05:36,850 --> 01:05:40,380
And whoever gets the most wins.

768
01:05:43,100 --> 01:05:44,890
I like that curve.

769
01:05:48,110 --> 01:05:49,890
It might sound boring,

770
01:05:50,570 --> 01:05:54,440
But I think the boring stuff is the stuff I remember the most.

771
01:06:01,950 --> 01:06:03,780
Look, there it is!

772
01:06:04,540 --> 01:06:07,950
Hold on, Russell, stand still.

773
01:06:18,550 --> 01:06:22,140
Look at that bird go! Wait up, you overgrown chicken!

774
01:06:23,430 --> 01:06:25,170
That's it! Go, Kevin!

775
01:06:25,170 --> 01:06:26,890
Go find your babies!

776
01:06:31,440 --> 01:06:33,270
Run, Kevin, run!

777
01:06:36,110 --> 01:06:37,440
Oh, no!

778
01:06:42,660 --> 01:06:44,900
Russell, give me your knife!

779
01:06:46,920 --> 01:06:48,910
Get away from my bird!

780
01:07:15,190 --> 01:07:16,310
No!

781
01:07:22,950 --> 01:07:24,240
No!

782
01:07:30,630 --> 01:07:33,490
Careful, I want it in good shape for my return.

783
01:07:35,300 --> 01:07:38,210
Let her go! Stop!

784
01:07:42,050 --> 01:07:43,960
Kevin!

785
01:07:57,690 --> 01:07:59,480
You gave away Kevin.

786
01:08:02,320 --> 01:08:05,160
You just gave her away.

787
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:09,620
This is none of my concern.

788
01:08:10,750 --> 01:08:12,580
I didn't ask for any of these!

789
01:08:15,250 --> 01:08:18,000
Master, it's all right.

790
01:08:18,840 --> 01:08:20,710
I am not your master!

791
01:08:21,430 --> 01:08:24,540
If you hadn't have shown up, none of these would have happened.

792
01:08:24,680 --> 01:08:26,920
Bad dog! Bad dog!

793
01:08:35,270 --> 01:08:37,360
Now, whether you assist me or not,

794
01:08:37,860 --> 01:08:41,440
I am going to paradise falls, if it kills me!

795
01:09:53,600 --> 01:09:57,440
Here. I don't want this anymore.

796
01:13:37,990 --> 01:13:39,150
Russell?

797
01:13:44,170 --> 01:13:45,200
Russell!

798
01:13:45,330 --> 01:13:49,050
I'm gonna help Kevin, even if you won't!

799
01:13:50,170 --> 01:13:52,160
No, Russell, no!

800
01:15:04,910 --> 01:15:06,070
Russell?

801
01:15:08,250 --> 01:15:09,360
Dug!

802
01:15:09,580 --> 01:15:12,700
I was hiding under your porch because I love you.

803
01:15:12,700 --> 01:15:14,200
Can I stay?

804
01:15:14,300 --> 01:15:16,710
Can you stay? Well, you're my dog, aren't you?

805
01:15:16,800 --> 01:15:18,130
And I'm your master.

806
01:15:18,260 --> 01:15:19,720
You're my master?

807
01:15:19,800 --> 01:15:21,130
Oh boy! Oh boy!

808
01:15:21,260 --> 01:15:24,000
Good boy, Dug! You're a good boy!

809
01:15:49,830 --> 01:15:50,950
Yes!

810
01:15:52,960 --> 01:15:54,790
Don't worry, Kevin, I'll save...

811
01:16:03,760 --> 01:16:06,000
And they wouldn't believe me.

812
01:16:06,000 --> 01:16:08,760
Just wait till they get a look at you!

813
01:16:08,850 --> 01:16:10,090
Master.

814
01:16:10,520 --> 01:16:13,640
- The small mailman has returned. - What?

815
01:16:14,150 --> 01:16:15,640
Let me go!

816
01:16:17,650 --> 01:16:19,610
Where is your elderly friend?

817
01:16:21,320 --> 01:16:23,530
He's not my friend anymore.

818
01:16:24,030 --> 01:16:27,490
Well, if you're here, Fredricksen can't be far behind.

819
01:16:28,500 --> 01:16:30,660
Where are you keeping Kevin?

820
01:16:31,830 --> 01:16:33,040
Let me go!

821
01:16:33,170 --> 01:16:35,330
Scream all you want, small mailman.

822
01:16:35,460 --> 01:16:37,830
None of your mailmen friends can hear you.

823
01:16:38,510 --> 01:16:42,000
I will unleash all my wilderness explorer training!

824
01:16:45,890 --> 01:16:47,500
Alfa, Fredricksen is coming back!

825
01:16:47,640 --> 01:16:48,730
Guard that bird.

826
01:16:48,730 --> 01:16:51,220
If you see the old man, you know what to do

827
01:16:51,350 --> 01:16:54,640
Hey, where are you going? I'm not finished with you!

828
01:16:54,730 --> 01:16:56,640
Nice talking with you.

829
01:17:01,530 --> 01:17:03,690
Where are you, Fredricksen?

830
01:17:18,750 --> 01:17:21,370
Help!

831
01:17:22,220 --> 01:17:23,550
Russell!

832
01:17:36,110 --> 01:17:38,720
- Mr. Fredricksen! - Dug, bring that over!

833
01:17:40,610 --> 01:17:43,100
You came back for Kevin! Let's go get her!

834
01:17:43,240 --> 01:17:45,400
I'm getting Kevin. You stay here.

835
01:17:45,530 --> 01:17:46,690
But I wanna help.

836
01:17:46,780 --> 01:17:48,070
I don't want your help.

837
01:17:48,200 --> 01:17:49,910
I want you safe.

838
01:17:57,080 --> 01:17:59,420
How do we get pass these dogs?

839
01:17:59,800 --> 01:18:01,130
Point!

840
01:18:11,600 --> 01:18:12,760
Kevin!

841
01:18:13,980 --> 01:18:16,430
Don't worry, Kevin. We are on our way.

842
01:18:16,940 --> 01:18:20,050
Allow no one should be enterring through these doors.

843
01:18:20,610 --> 01:18:23,150
Guard well that bird, my minions.

844
01:18:24,070 --> 01:18:25,480
What do we do now, Dug?

845
01:18:38,790 --> 01:18:40,620
Who wants the ball?

846
01:18:41,840 --> 01:18:43,620
- Me. I want it! - Me. I do!

847
01:18:43,960 --> 01:18:45,330
- I want the ball! - Give it to me!

848
01:18:45,470 --> 01:18:46,710
Then go get it!

849
01:18:46,800 --> 01:18:49,170
I'm gonna get there first!

850
01:18:49,300 --> 01:18:50,670
Getting the ball!

851
01:18:50,800 --> 01:18:52,260
I got it!

852
01:18:52,640 --> 01:18:53,630
Uh-oh.

853
01:18:57,480 --> 01:19:00,390
I'm sorry, Kevin. Let's get you out of here.

854
01:19:00,480 --> 01:19:03,300
- Master! He's gone! The old man! - What's going on?

855
01:19:03,300 --> 01:19:05,810
- He's here! - He's got the bird! - The bird's gone...

856
01:19:05,950 --> 01:19:07,940
Calm down! One at a time!

857
01:19:11,450 --> 01:19:14,190
I want...to...help!

858
01:19:24,840 --> 01:19:26,290
- He's in Hall D! - He's in Hall C!

859
01:19:26,380 --> 01:19:27,840
It's the old man!

860
01:19:28,220 --> 01:19:31,250
Does anyone know where they are?

861
01:19:46,820 --> 01:19:49,060
Gray Leader? Take down the house.

862
01:19:55,830 --> 01:19:57,110
Gray Leader checking in.

863
01:19:57,200 --> 01:19:58,190
Gray Two, checking in.

864
01:19:58,330 --> 01:19:59,490
Gray Three, checking in.

865
01:20:04,000 --> 01:20:05,330
Target sighted.

866
01:20:13,800 --> 01:20:15,340
Come on, Kevin.

867
01:20:30,400 --> 01:20:31,560
Hi.

868
01:20:57,850 --> 01:20:59,790
Any Iast words, Fredricksen?

869
01:20:59,790 --> 01:21:01,180
Come on! Spit it out!

870
01:21:04,940 --> 01:21:07,180
- Come on. - Enough

871
01:21:07,520 --> 01:21:12,230
I am taking that bird back with me. Alive or dead.

872
01:21:38,560 --> 01:21:40,220
Come on, Kevin.

873
01:21:59,450 --> 01:22:02,410
I will have many enjoyments from what I am about to do, Dug.

874
01:22:10,800 --> 01:22:12,290
He wears the Cone of Shame!

875
01:22:12,840 --> 01:22:16,250
What? Do not just continue sitting. Attack!

876
01:22:19,350 --> 01:22:21,280
No, no! Stop your laughing!

877
01:22:21,280 --> 01:22:22,590
Get this off of me!

878
01:22:22,680 --> 01:22:24,590
Listen, you dog. Sit!

879
01:22:26,190 --> 01:22:27,430
Yes, Alpha.

880
01:22:27,520 --> 01:22:30,140
Alpha? I am not Alpha. He is....

881
01:22:30,520 --> 01:22:31,560
Oh!

882
01:22:33,190 --> 01:22:34,900
I can't do it.

883
01:22:37,240 --> 01:22:38,480
Russell.

884
01:22:43,000 --> 01:22:45,490
You leave Mr. Fredricksen alone!

885
01:23:02,220 --> 01:23:04,090
Hey! Squirrel!

886
01:23:04,180 --> 01:23:05,360
SquirreI? Where? Where? Where?

887
01:23:05,360 --> 01:23:07,600
Where's the squirrel?

888
01:23:11,440 --> 01:23:13,100
I hate squirrels!

889
01:23:33,800 --> 01:23:34,880
Dug!

890
01:23:35,380 --> 01:23:36,590
Master!

891
01:23:37,630 --> 01:23:40,970
Russell, over here! Let's go!

892
01:23:45,810 --> 01:23:47,640
Mr. Fredricksen!

893
01:23:48,230 --> 01:23:49,840
Go on, Kevin.

894
01:24:04,790 --> 01:24:05,900
No!

895
01:24:20,760 --> 01:24:23,090
Russell, get out of there!

896
01:24:25,100 --> 01:24:27,210
No. Leave them alone!

897
01:24:42,530 --> 01:24:46,700
Russell, hang on to kevin! Don't let go of her.

898
01:24:48,790 --> 01:24:50,870
Kevin! Chocolate!

899
01:25:13,400 --> 01:25:15,010
That was cool!

900
01:25:17,070 --> 01:25:21,430
Don't jerk around so much, kid. Easy Russell.

901
01:25:23,740 --> 01:25:26,230
Oh, I am ready to not be up high.

902
01:25:49,600 --> 01:25:52,260
Sorry about your house, Mr. Fredricksen.

903
01:25:54,900 --> 01:25:57,680
You know, its just a house.

904
01:26:05,740 --> 01:26:07,900
Look at you. You're so soft.

905
01:26:12,160 --> 01:26:13,950
I wish I could keep one.

906
01:26:18,340 --> 01:26:20,370
Where is my cane? I just had it here.

907
01:26:28,640 --> 01:26:31,970
You know what? Keep them. A little gift from me to you.

908
01:26:32,850 --> 01:26:34,390
Bye Kevin!

909
01:26:43,820 --> 01:26:45,100
Ready?

910
01:26:45,490 --> 01:26:46,820
Ready.

911
01:26:57,580 --> 01:26:59,320
And by receiving their badges,

912
01:26:59,420 --> 01:27:04,080
The following Explorers will graduate to Senior Explorers.

913
01:27:04,460 --> 01:27:08,300
For Extreme Mountaineering Lore. Congratulations. Jimmy.

914
01:27:08,550 --> 01:27:13,010
For Wild Animal Defensive Arts. Congratulations. Brandon.

915
01:27:13,520 --> 01:27:15,680
For Assistlng the Elderly....

916
01:27:16,520 --> 01:27:19,680
Uh, Russe , is there someone that....

917
01:27:22,440 --> 01:27:25,520
Excuse me. Pardon me. Old man coming through.

918
01:27:28,360 --> 01:27:29,850
I'm here for him.

919
01:27:30,070 --> 01:27:32,310
Congratulations, Russell. Sir.

920
01:27:35,500 --> 01:27:38,580
Russell, for Assisting the Elderly

921
01:27:39,040 --> 01:27:43,250
And for performing above and beyond the call of duty,

922
01:27:44,210 --> 01:27:48,500
I would like to award you the highest honor I can bestow.

923
01:27:50,890 --> 01:27:52,630
The Ellie Badge.

924
01:28:01,440 --> 01:28:03,930
All right. I think that covers everybody.

925
01:28:04,020 --> 01:28:06,060
So let's give a big explorer call

926
01:28:06,360 --> 01:28:09,850
To our brand new Senior Wilderness Explorers.

927
01:28:10,110 --> 01:28:11,230
Ready, everybody?

928
01:28:19,920 --> 01:28:21,620
- Blue one. - Red one

929
01:28:22,290 --> 01:28:24,080
- Blue one. - Gray one.

930
01:28:25,050 --> 01:28:27,040
- Red one. - That's a bike.

931
01:28:27,460 --> 01:28:29,130
It's red, isn't it?

932
01:28:29,220 --> 01:28:31,080
Mr. Fredricksen, you're cheating.

933
01:28:31,300 --> 01:28:33,090
No, I'm not. Red one.

934
01:28:33,180 --> 01:28:34,960
That's a fire hydrant.

935
01:28:37,100 --> 01:28:39,130
Maybe I need new lessons.

936
01:28:39,480 --> 01:28:41,090
Another blue one.

